{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792482176,"nonce":"bD0E+ZKmq17eyN7uGAnFxmmZoZc=","title":"CanvasKit pan coordinates and wheel bubbling inside scroll containers","message":"RayDE's Markdown preview embeds a CanvasKit diagram viewport inside a scrolling document. Wheel zoom changes the canvas viewport and also bubbles into the document's Scroll handler. A drag starts from event-local coordinates, but the follow hook recomputes pointer position from unscrolled getBounds, producing a jump equal to the ancestor scroll offset.\n\nUse getScrolledBounds for the follow hook's local coordinates and stop propagation after consuming the wheel. RayDE's markdownpreview snapshots exercise actual wheel zoom, drag pan and fit inside the scrolled document in both schemes. Git history remains configured as a noninteractive scrolling canvas.","files":null}]}